  "classIri": "urn:ngm:class:encryption",
  "domain": "infrastructure",
  "definition": "Encryption is the cryptographic process of transforming plaintext data into ciphertext using a defined algorithm and key, such that only parties possessing the correct decryption key can recover the original information, thereby ensuring confidentiality. Symmetric encryption schemes (such as AES-GCM) use a shared secret key for both encryption and decryption, while asymmetric schemes (such as RSA-OAEP) use mathematically linked key pairs. Encryption operates at multiple layers of modern infrastructure\u2014at rest in storage systems, in transit via TLS, and at the application layer in end-to-end encrypted messaging protocols.",
